// XFAIL: RT-39: indexing a raw slice `*mut [T]` / `*const [T]` needs no `unsafe`: a use after free and a write through `&` in safe code (open)
// `q[0] = 7` of a `q: *mut [i64]` is an index through a raw pointer, and
// vole takes it as safe: synth_index asks for `unsafe` only of a
// TyKind::Ptr, and a raw slice is a TyKind::Slice with REF_RAW. Here q
// points into a Vec dropped when mk returns: at -O0 --check-alloc the
// write is "use after free: block #1 (32 bytes), allocated at line 16,
// freed at line 19". rustc refuses the index (E0608: cannot index into a
// value of type `*mut [i64]`); vole should ask for `unsafe` (or refuse it
// as rustc does). Pre-existing in 0.30.0; found by the review of the RT-33
// branch.
// ERROR: error[
// ERROR: line 23,
// ERROR-COUNT: 1
fn mk(gpa: Gpa) -> *mut [i64] {
    let mut v: Vec<i64, Gpa> = Vec::new_in(gpa);
    v.push(1);
    v.push(2);
    &mut v[..] as *mut [i64]
}

fn main(gpa: Gpa) {
    let q = mk(gpa);
    q[0] = 7;
}
